Lina: quick FYI - nightly billing shows big usage on org default projects. looks like projectless keys are being attributed to the default project in analytics.
Marco: yep. router sets effective_project=org.default_project when no project claim. good for quotas but bad for billing provenance.
Jules: we should split routing vs attribution. emit `project.effective` for enforcement and `project.provenance` tag for telemetry (asserted|claim|fallback).
Anya: security: if we accept an asserted value it must be verifiable. plan: auth-service emits `x-project-assertion` (compact signed JWT). gateway verifies signature, then emits provenance=asserted but still uses effective_project for quota.
Marco: pseudo:
```
if verifyJwt('x-project-assertion') {
  provenance='asserted'; project=jwt.project
} else if (token.claims.project) {
  provenance='claim'; project=token.claims.project
} else {
  provenance='fallback'; project=org.default_project
}
emit('request.attribution', project, provenance)
```
Lina: rollout: feature flag `attrib_assertions`. staging -> 5% canary -> monitor attribution deltas and billing pipeline. coordinate with finance for backfill.
Anya: security checklist: signed by auth-service key, ttl<=5s, jti for replay prevention, gateway verification and audit logging.
Jules: console UX: add "Source" badge (ASSERTED/CLAIM/FALLBACK) and default filter to hide FALLBACK entries.
ops-bot: feature flag attrib_assertions enabled in staging :white_check_mark:
Lina: action items: Marco/gateway changes, Jules/console mock, Anya/signature spec, Lina/sync with finance. target canary next week. thanks.
